.TH CONVT-APP 1 "2026-10-04" "convt 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
convt-app \- desktop file converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B convt-app open
.RI [ "--to format" ] " -- files"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open selected files in Quick convert. Choose an available format, follow
progress and cancel conversions. An X11 or Wayland desktop and a working
Vulkan driver are required. If the window cannot open, convt prints the
error, writes
.I window-error.log
in its config directory, shows a zenity or kdialog dialog when one is
available, and exits with status 1 if no other window is open and no
conversion is running. On Linux that first failure retries once with Mesa
lavapipe when that ICD is installed. A later Settings or Quick convert
failure leaves the running session alone.
Use --help for all entry points, including convt:// URLs.
.PP
AppImage and tarball builds include the file-manager menu installer. Open
Settings and choose
.B Set up right-click menu
to install per-user menus for GNOME Files, Dolphin, Nemo and Thunar.
Menus written from an AppImage launch that AppImage file, not its
temporary mount.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR convt (1)
